<speak>With Pioneer Balanced Opportunities Fund, the bond holdings can fall in value when interest rates rise, and the equity holdings can fall when stock markets weaken. During stressed markets, those holdings can decline together, reducing the protection diversification provides. Your capital is not protected in this investment. You could lose some or all of the capital you invest. Do you understand those risks, including that the fund's equity and bond holdings can fall together despite its diversification?</speak>